.TH CODEX-TERMUX 1 "2026-10-28" "codex-termux 0.4.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
codex-termux \- run and maintain Codex in native Android Termux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B codex-termux
.RI [ wrapper-options ]
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ arguments ...]
.br
.B codex-termux manage self-update
.RI [ package-options ]
.br
.B codex-termux manage uninstall
.RI [ package-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the Linux ARM64 or x64 npm build of Codex using native Termux Node.js
for DNS through a temporary loopback CONNECT proxy. No proot or persistent
proxy service is required. TLS verification remains enabled.
.PP
Wrapper options precede the command. Unknown commands and options are passed
to Codex. Arguments after run or chatgpt are passed through without shell
evaluation. The default command is run.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Launch Codex. Also bypasses wrapper-reserved command names.
.TP
.B chatgpt
Launch with OPENAI_API_KEY, CODEX_API_KEY, and CODEX_ACCESS_TOKEN removed
from the child environment. Stored authentication remains controlled by Codex.
.TP
.B login
Use ChatGPT device authorization by default. Extra arguments go to Codex login.
.TP
.B login-api
Pass OPENAI_API_KEY to Codex on standard input, not as an argument.
.TP
.B status
Show Codex authentication status.
.TP
.B logout
Remove stored Codex credentials using Codex logout.
.TP
.B doctor
Run Codex doctor \-\-all, or the supplied doctor options.
.TP
.B test
Check Node DNS, proxied HTTPS transport, and Codex Doctor. An HTTP response
from the auth root is not proof of successful login.
.TP
.B setup [\-\-yes] [\-\-version X.Y.Z]
Check/install missing Termux dependencies and prepare a Codex npm runtime.
Package operations require confirmation or explicit \-\-yes.
.TP
.B completion bash|zsh
Write a static completion script. No extension, Codex, or network execution
is performed during generation or completion.
.SH MAINTENANCE
.TP
.B manage check [\-\-json]
Inspect local prerequisites and Codex version.
.TP
.B manage auth-check [\-\-json]
Inspect the last 256 KiB of an existing diagnostic log for MCP HTTP 401
token_expired errors. This is saved evidence, not a live authentication test.
JSON contains fixed status/server fields and a timestamp, never log text.
No match does not establish healthy authentication.
.TP
.B manage update [\-\-check [\-\-json]] [\-\-yes] [\-\-version X.Y.Z]
Check or update the Codex npm runtime, with exact matching launcher/native
packages, staging, smoke tests, and an atomic selection record.
The global npm installation remains unchanged.
.TP
.B manage rollback [\-\-yes]
Validate and select the previous Codex npm runtime.
.TP
.B manage self-update [package-options]
Check or update this wrapper package, including Bash/Zsh completions and
the manual. This is separate from manage update.
.TP
.B manage uninstall [\-\-dry-run] [\-\-yes] [\-\-prefix DIR] [\-\-color MODE] [\-\-output MODE]
Remove verified package-managed public entries after confirmation.
Preserve Codex runtimes, authentication, configuration, shell startup,
recovery backups, and private package history.
.TP
.B manage config show|example
Print effective nonsecret settings or a literal configuration template.
.SH TERMUX SERVICE MANAGEMENT
Runit is the default backend for both manage server and connect.
Existing explicit connect_backend=managed configuration remains honored.
The precedence is command --backend, CODEX_TERMUX_CONNECT_BACKEND, literal
connect_backend configuration, then the runit default. No fallback is attempted.
.PP
.B manage server start|stop|restart [--wait N] [--backend runit|managed]
uses sv -w N with the matching action. The wait defaults to 20 seconds;
--wait/-w accepts 1 through 300. Native exit status and raw output are preserved;
timeouts do not trigger forced termination. Autostart is unchanged.
A rapid restart can return before a subsequent status observes the replacement.
.PP
.B manage server status
runs sv status, with readable terminal fields or native raw output.
Success can describe a stopped service.
.PP
.B manage server enable|disable [--wait N]
removes or creates the service down marker, then starts or stops the service.
This matches the Termux sv-enable/sv-disable convention with bounded waits.
The autostart setting remains changed if lifecycle control fails; an error
reports that setting. Autostart refers to service supervisor startup, not an
Android reboot or process-survival guarantee.
.PP
.B manage server is-enabled
shows Enabled (exit 0) or Disabled (exit 1), or lowercase scalar output in raw
mode. Missing or unsafe state is an error.
.PP
.B manage server logs [--lines N] [--follow]
reads $HOME/.local/share/codex-remote/log/current. --lines/-n selects 1 through
10000 lines (default 100); --follow/-f follows rotation until Ctrl+C.
Only existing logs are read; no additional recording or service action occurs.
.PP
.B manage server check
reports runit status and validates the private token, authenticated WebSocket
upgrade, and rejection without authentication. It needs Node but no selected
Codex runtime; it launches no Codex client and never prints the token.
Success does not verify account health. Lifecycle/status/autostart/logs/help
need no Node, npm, or Codex.
.PP
.B manage server help
shows command and option help. --help/-h also works after a subcommand.
All server operations except help accept --backend runit|managed. The managed backend
supports only start/status/stop; its start requires --auth and accepts --port.
Runit rejects those options because auth/port belong to the service definition.
.PP
The fixed service is codex-remote under absolute $SVDIR, or $PREFIX/var/service
when SVDIR is empty/unset. Its directory must be owned and not a symlink.
Existing down markers must be owned regular files, not symlinks; disabling
never overwrites their content. No service installation, global supervisor
start, script rewrite, credential change, or migration is implicit.
.SH RUNIT CONNECTIONS
.B connect [--backend runit|managed] [--chatgpt] [--] [CODEX_ARGUMENTS...]
selects the configured backend; leading --backend and --chatgpt can appear in
either order before Codex arguments or the optional wrapper delimiter.
Runit requires --chatgpt. Ordinary launches are never rerouted.
The endpoint is ws://127.0.0.1:4511; runit_port or CODEX_TERMUX_RUNIT_PORT
can override the port. The token is $HOME/.local/share/codex-remote/token.
The directory and regular token file must be owner-only and not symlinks.
No proxy or service is started by connect. Authentication is checked before
launch; failure never falls back. Keep server/client Codex versions aligned;
this backend has no managed runtime fingerprint.
.SH LEGACY MANAGED APP SERVER
.B manage server start --backend managed --auth inherited|chatgpt [--port N]
starts an opt-in detached app server and native Node DNS/CONNECT proxy.
Only 127.0.0.1 with capability-token authentication is supported. The default
port is temporary; external port 4500 is reserved and rejected.
This is a WebSocket workaround, not a repair of the upstream Unix-socket daemon.
.PP
.B manage server status --backend managed
verifies the live supervisor, authenticated WebSocket upgrade and unauthenticated
rejection, and reports auth/runtime identity. This does not verify account health.
.B manage server stop --backend managed
asks the verified supervisor to stop its own server and proxy, even if the
selected runtime is missing. Stop ends active server work.
.PP
.B connect --backend managed [--chatgpt] [--] [CODEX_ARGUMENTS...]
connects to the managed instance, including resume and fork arguments.
Preserves argument boundaries, cwd (overridable with --cd/-C), terminal streams,
exit status and interrupt continuation. Rejects forwarded --remote,
--remote-auth-token-env and --no-daemon before Codex's own -- delimiter.
The first optional leading -- belongs to the wrapper. A subsequent -- and all
following positional arguments are forwarded unchanged; option-like prompt text
there does not suppress the default cwd. Ordinary launches are never rerouted.
.PP
The inherited mode retains start-time credentials and requires matching
OPENAI_API_KEY, CODEX_API_KEY and CODEX_ACCESS_TOKEN presence/values on connect.
The chatgpt mode removes these variables, and requires connect --backend managed --chatgpt.
A client cannot change server authentication. Saved auth remains Codex-controlled.
Other provider environment/config changes require an explicit restart after work
finishes; dynamic custom-provider credential switching is unsupported.
.PP
Instance selection is the wrapper data directory plus canonical CODEX_HOME
(default HOME/.codex, an existing absolute directory). Existing wrapper path,
CA, proxy and runtime overrides are honored. Private servers/home-hash state uses
0700 directories and 0600 files. Tokens are never printed or put in arguments.
The client receives a token through its environment. Same-user processes are
within the trust boundary.
.PP
Duplicate starts and uncertain ownership/state are refused. Startup waits up to
12 seconds for readiness, five seconds for cleanup, and 20 seconds in the caller.
Raw server output is discarded; diagnostics contain only fixed events.
Stop never signals a saved PID. Surviving state after a forced kill requires
owner review; no automatic adoption, stale-state deletion or force kill exists.
A runtime mismatch is reported by status and refused by connect. Update/rollback
do not restart the server or delete its runtime.
.PP
The server/proxy survive client exit and starting-shell closure. Android may
still kill them under memory/battery pressure. No force-stop/reboot survival,
automatic restart, wake lock or boot service is promised. If the supervisor is
forcibly killed, its child may survive and state must be reviewed.
.PP
Recovery: codex-termux --wrapper-no-update chatgpt --no-daemon
(or run --no-daemon to retain API variables). See README for candidate and
owner-run model-response, pwd, resume and stop acceptance sequences.
.SH WRAPPER OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show colored, terminal-aware help.
.TP
.B \-\-wrapper-version
Print the wrapper version without starting Node. Bare \-\-version continues
to select Codex's version.
.TP
.B \-\-wrapper-info [\-\-json]
Print local runtime information. JSON has no color or banner.
.TP
.B \-\-wrapper-dry-run
Describe run/chatgpt without executing it. Other actions are refused.
For package previews, use manage self-update \-\-dry-run instead.
.TP
.B \-\-wrapper-no-update
Disable automatic Codex npm update checks and prompts for this launch.
Explicit maintenance commands remain available.
.TP
.B \-\-wrapper-color auto|always|never
Select output color. Automatic color honors NO_COLOR and terminal detection.
.TP
.B \-\-wrapper-output auto|pretty|raw
Select human report layout. Auto formats terminal streams except TERM=dumb
and preserves existing redirected contracts. Pretty forces layout without
forcing color. Raw bypasses formatting and wrapper colors/banners even when
color or banner is always. JSON and literal protocols are never formatted.
.TP
.B \-\-wrapper-banner auto|always|never
Control the responsive ASCII header.
.TP
.B \-\-wrapper-config PATH
Read an explicit literal key=value configuration file.
.TP
.B \-\-wrapper-no-config
Ignore the configuration file.
.TP
.B \-\-wrapper-debug
Emit fixed wrapper events on stderr without argument values or credentials.
.SH OUTPUT STYLE AND COMPLETION
Root and server help share responsive banner controls, bold cyan branding,
bold magenta headings, bold green command rows, bold yellow option rows,
and white descriptions. Help rows use two-space indentation and a minimum
27-column label field. Package help uses the same roles with compact branding.
.PP
Automatic color is disabled for redirected output, TERM=dumb, or NO_COLOR.
Explicit always forces human-output color even in those cases; never disables
it unless output is explicitly raw. Package --color and --output can override
the wrapper's effective settings. NO_COLOR retains readable report layout.
stdout and stderr detect their terminals independently.
.PP
Human reports use compact headings and aligned label/value rows, stacked below
60 columns. Success/active states are green, warnings/inactive states yellow,
and failures red; status words also convey their meaning without color.
Service reports retain native details and producer exit codes, including
unknown formats. Logs highlight leading timestamps and severity fields without
filtering, truncating, or reordering messages. Pretty logs remove incoming ANSI
SGR styling before applying the wrapper palette. Consecutive logger/Codex
timestamps, including underscore timestamps, are retained. Other terminal
controls remain visible escapes; literal backslash text is not decoded.
Raw mode preserves original bytes, including unterminated lines.
Following logs preserves rotation and Ctrl+C/TERM cleanup without service control.
.PP
JSON, configuration examples, emitted completion scripts, version scalars,
internal helper data, and forwarded Codex streams remain literal. Config show
uses readable rows in pretty mode and literal key/value lines in raw mode.
Raw service/log output and automatic redirected service/log output preserve
native bytes. Top-level status/doctor remain Codex-owned output.
.PP
Bash and Zsh completion respect an explicitly supplied server backend. With no
explicit backend they offer the applicable union, because completion never
reads configuration or performs runtime/service discovery. Zsh describes
backend-only options. Server/connect completion omits already-used single-use
options, including short/long aliases, and stops at forwarding boundaries.
.SH PACKAGE INSTALLATION
Run install.sh from a built checkout for a local installation.
When no checkout is detected, it downloads published GitHub Release assets.
Use \-\-remote to request Releases explicitly, or \-\-source DIR for a
built source directory. The default destination is Termux's PREFIX.
.PP
The installer compares stable numeric wrapper versions. Equal versions exit
without replacement. An older offered version never downgrades the installation.
Use \-\-repair to recreate missing managed links at the same version.
.PP
Payload files are checked against a strict SHA256SUMS manifest. The manifest
and downloads use HTTPS from the same release; this provides integrity under
the trust placed in the repository and HTTPS, not independent signing.
Release files are never executed to discover their version.
.PP
Package options: \-\-prefix DIR, \-\-source DIR, \-\-remote,
\-\-version X.Y.Z, \-\-check, \-\-dry-run, \-\-repair,
\-\-recover, \-\-yes, \-\-color auto|always|never, and \-\-output auto|pretty|raw.
Standalone tools honor CODEX_TERMUX_OUTPUT but do not read wrapper config.
Delegated tools inherit the wrapper mode unless explicitly overridden.
The prefix must already exist and be owned by the current user.
.PP
Confirmation reads /dev/tty even when the script itself is piped from curl
or wget. In an unattended environment an explicit \-\-yes is required.
.PP
New payloads are immutable versioned directories. Public symlinks point through
one current pointer, so normal updates switch all components together.
Initial installation/adoption and uninstallation involve several directory
entries. An ordinary failure rolls these back using recorded backups.
After an interrupted transaction, review pending state and use
install.sh \-\-recover. Do not remove an operation lock without checking
that its owner has stopped.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Optional configuration is read from
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/codex-termux/config, or $HOME/.config/codex-termux/config.
It is literal data, never sourced or evaluated. Use absolute literal paths.
Precedence is wrapper prefix options, environment, configuration, defaults.
.PP
Keys: auto_update=ask|notify|off, update_interval=86400,
color=auto|always|never, banner=auto|always|never, output=auto|pretty|raw,
proxy_connect_timeout=10000, proxy_allow, codex_bin, ca_bundle,
connect_backend=runit|managed (default runit), and runit_port=4511.
The interval is seconds; connection timeout is milliseconds.
.PP
auth_notice=auto|off controls post-session token-expiry notices.
auth_log selects an absolute existing diagnostic-log path.
By default, use $CODEX_HOME/log/codex-tui.log or
$HOME/.codex/log/codex-tui.log when CODEX_HOME is unset.
.SH AUTHENTICATION NOTICES
After an eligible interactive run/chatgpt session exits, inspect up to the first
256 KiB added to its existing diagnostic log during that launch.
Recognized MCP warning/error records with HTTP 401 and token_expired produce
a recovery hint. When the record identifies codex_apps, suggest logout,
login, and chatgpt; otherwise make that advice conditional on the failed server.
Never execute recovery commands automatically.
.PP
No startup network probe, credential-store read, stream interception,
logging configuration change, or background watcher is added.
Only recognized interactive launch grammar with all three streams on terminals
enables the automatic notice. Redirected output, exec, login and unknown grammar
skip it. Codex exit status and signal handling remain unchanged.
.PP
Old entries are ignored automatically. Observed rotation/truncation, unsafe or
unreadable logs are skipped. A custom Codex log directory needs an explicit
auth_log setting; Codex configuration layers are not parsed.
Disabled logging, changed log formats, bounded reads and concurrent sessions
sharing one log limit detection. Existing errors can predate a successful login.
Explicit auth-check reports unavailable logs without a login-health conclusion.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SVDIR
Absolute services directory; defaults to $PREFIX/var/service.
The server commands target its codex-remote directory.
.TP
.B CODEX_TERMUX_CONNECT_BACKEND
Select runit or managed for management and connections; --backend overrides it.
.TP
.B CODEX_TERMUX_RUNIT_PORT
Existing loopback endpoint port for runit connections/checks; default 4511.
This does not change the service definition.
.TP
.B PREFIX
Termux installation prefix; package tools install below this prefix by default.
.TP
.B CODEX_TERMUX_CODEX_BIN
Explicit executable override. Managed npm installation is disabled with an override.
.TP
.B CODEX_TERMUX_PROXY_ALLOW
Comma-separated extra permitted proxy hostname trees.
.TP
.B CODEX_TERMUX_AUTO_UPDATE
ask, notify, or off. Eligible interactive launches use cached npm update metadata.
Automatic checking never installs without confirmation. Wrapper package updates
are explicit through manage self-update.
.TP
.B CODEX_TERMUX_AUTH_NOTICE
auto (default) or off. Disable automatic log-based notices with off.
.TP
.B CODEX_TERMUX_AUTH_LOG
Override the existing diagnostic-log path. Does not enable Codex logging.
.TP
.B CODEX_TERMUX_UPDATE_INTERVAL
Successful npm metadata lifetime, from 3600 through 2592000 seconds.
.TP
.B CODEX_TERMUX_COLOR, CODEX_TERMUX_BANNER
Override wrapper color/header modes.
.TP
.B CODEX_TERMUX_OUTPUT
Override human output mode (auto, pretty, raw). Wrapper --wrapper-output or
package --output takes precedence. The default is auto.
.TP
.B CODEX_TERMUX_PROXY_CONNECT_TIMEOUT
TCP connection-establishment deadline, 1000 through 120000 milliseconds.
Established streaming tunnels have no added lifetime cutoff.
.TP
.B CODEX_TERMUX_CONFIG, CODEX_TERMUX_CA_BUNDLE
Explicit configuration or Codex/curl certificate-bundle path.
.TP
.B CODEX_TERMUX_DATA_DIR, CODEX_TERMUX_CACHE_DIR
Override private npm-runtime and update-cache locations.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable automatic color. An explicit always mode overrides automatic detection.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B $PREFIX/bin/codex-termux
Installed command link.
.TP
.B $PREFIX/share/bash-completion/completions/codex-termux
Bash completion link.
.TP
.B $PREFIX/share/zsh/site-functions/_codex-termux
Zsh completion link. Reload completion after first installation if needed.
.TP
.B $PREFIX/share/man/man1/codex-termux.1
This manual.
.TP
.B $PREFIX/libexec/codex-termux
Private wrapper package releases, current pointer, and recovery snapshots.
.TP
.B $XDG_DATA_HOME/codex-termux
Managed Codex npm runtimes; defaults under $HOME/.local/share.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
codex-termux chatgpt
codex-termux manage auth-check
codex-termux manage auth-check --json
codex-termux manage update --check
codex-termux manage self-update --check
codex-termux manage self-update
codex-termux manage uninstall --dry-run
bash install.sh --source . --dry-run
bash install.sh --source .
bash uninstall.sh
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Core success returns 0, operational failure 1, and wrapper usage errors 2.
Runit lifecycle/status commands preserve sv exit codes. is-enabled returns
1 when disabled; check returns nonzero on supervision or authentication failure.
A started Codex command preserves its exit status. Package no-ops and declined
confirmations return 0. Package operational errors return 1, usage errors 2.
Auth-check returns 0 for no matching saved evidence, 1 for expiry evidence,
2 for usage errors, and 3 for an unavailable log. No match is not verified login.
.SH LIMITATIONS
The wrapper does not change models, approval policy, OS sandbox settings,
credentials, or shell startup. It does not supply bubblewrap or make unsupported
Android sandbox features available. A proxy allowlist is not a network sandbox.
Forced process termination can prevent cleanup; surviving locks require review.
Native Termux behavior must be checked on the user's device.
